d of 100. My cards? Ace of Spades, Ten of Spades (ATs). Pre-flop, the board is clean.\n\nGiven the valid actions (Fold, All-In, Check, Raise, anything above 200), and my position, I need to make a strategic decision. With ATs suited in heads-up play, I have a strong hand. It\'s a premium hand that I definitely want to play.\n\nFirst, I quickly ruled out folding as an option. Not with this hand. Checking is an option, but it\'s too passive in this spot. I really want to build the pot and take the initiative. Going all-in is a bit too risky at this stage.\n\nA standard move here is to raise. The prompt suggests "200 (raise)", which is a min-raise (2x big blind). I\'m leaning toward a raise, especially since the prompt listed 200 as a valid raise. But a raise of 2.5-3 big blinds (250-300) is also standard.\n\nThe "0 (Check)" option is a little puzzling because, as the small blind, I don\'t get to check pre-flop unless the big blind just limps. I\'m assuming that "0" is intended to mean "Call". However, given my hand, I believe a raise is the strongest play.\n\nWith Ace-Ten suited, I have excellent potential. I have high-card value and flush/straight possibilities. In heads-up, this is a very strong starting hand, and I want to exploit that edge. A raise will extract value and build the pot. I want to build the pot when I\'m likely ahead.\n\nTherefore, after considering all the options, I\'m going to raise. I will raise to 200, but I could raise to 250/300 since a 2.5/3x BB raise is more standard.\n\n\n', 'output': 'Evaluation: Ace-Ten suited (As 10s) is a very strong hand in a heads-up scenario, possessing both high card strength and significant potential for flushes and straights. It has excellent equity against a random hand and performs well post-flop.\n\nReason: Playing passively (calling/checking) allows the opponent to see a flop for free or cheap with weak hands. Raising is the optimal strategy to build the pot for value, take the initiative, and potentially take down the pot pre-flop. A minimum raise to 200 is a standard, effective play here.\n\nAnswer: 200'}
