\n\nReason: Betting (donk betting) into the aggressor is risky with a middle pair; it tends to fold out worse hands while getting called or raised by better hands (like a King). Checking is the standard play here to control the pot size. It keeps the opponent\'s bluffs in their range and allows you to see the river or react to their bet without over-committing chips with a marginal hand.\n\nAnswer: 0'}
